# Calls every endpoint of a running instance: `docker compose up` (port 8080) or the "http" launch profile (port 5290).
# Visual Studio (17.12+) and VS Code (REST Client) take the token from the "login" request.
# Rider takes it from "login-rider", whose handler sets a global variable that overrides @token.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Health (anonymous)
GET {{host}}/health

### Log in (Visual Studio, VS Code)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/mock-login
Content-Type: application/json

{"user": "valid"}

### Log in (Rider)
# @name login-rider
POST {{host}}/mock-login
Content-Type: application/json

{"user": "valid"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### Every place named Athens in Greece, nearest to the Acropolis first
GET {{host}}/city-report/GR/Athens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filters and sorting: Crete only, warmest first, weather hours of the window, latest first
GET {{host}}/city-report/GR/Chania?region=crete&sort=-temperature&include=weather,hourly&hourly.category=weather&hourly.sort=-time
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Degraded: Ioannina is inland, so the marine API has nothing for it (sources.marine = no_data) while the rest is ok
GET {{host}}/city-report/GR/Ioannina
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 404: no such city or airport
GET {{host}}/city-report/GR/Xyzqwerty
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 400: sort=temperature needs include=weather
GET {{host}}/city-report/GR/Athens?include=airQuality&sort=temperature
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Statistics per external API
GET {{host}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 401: no token
GET {{host}}/stats
